# 42. Definition of Done — MVP

The MVP is considered complete when:

* [ ] Users can register.
* [ ] Users can log in.
* [ ] Users can browse courses.
* [ ] Users can view course details.
* [ ] Users can start checkout.
* [ ] Users can complete payment.
* [ ] The system receives payment webhooks.
* [ ] The system verifies payments.
* [ ] Enrollment is automatically created.
* [ ] Users can access purchased courses.
* [ ] Users can watch YouTube videos.
* [ ] Users can complete lessons.
* [ ] Progress is stored.
* [ ] Users can resume their last lesson.
* [ ] Admins can create courses.
* [ ] Admins can create modules.
* [ ] Admins can create lessons.
* [ ] Admins can add YouTube Video IDs.
* [ ] Admins can set course prices.
* [ ] Admins can view transactions.
* [ ] Admins can view users.
* [ ] Access control works correctly.
* [ ] The website is responsive.
* [ ] Error handling is implemented.
* [ ] The application is deployed to production.

---

# 43. Product KPIs

At the beginning, avoid tracking too many metrics.

Focus on these five:

| KPI                       | Purpose                        |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Visitor → Registration    | Measure user interest          |
| Registration → Purchase   | Measure conversion             |
| Purchase → Course Start   | Measure activation             |
| Course Start → Completion | Measure learning effectiveness |
| Repeat Purchase           | Measure product value          |

### Recommended North Star Metric

> **Number of students who successfully complete meaningful learning outcomes.**

The product should not optimize merely for the number of videos watched.

---

# 44. Core Product Principle

The most important strategic principle is:

**Do not build this product as "a website containing paid YouTube videos."**

That would create relatively little defensible value and would be easy to replicate.

Instead, build it as:

> **An Arabic Language Learning Management System.**

YouTube is simply the **video delivery mechanism**.

The core value should come from:

```text
Video
   +
Curriculum
   +
Learning Path
   +
Progress Tracking
   +
Exercises
   +
Assessment
   +
Learning Resources
   =
Arabic Learning Platform
```

This positioning allows the product to eventually evolve from a **paid YouTube course platform** into a much more valuable **Arabic Learning LMS**.

---

# 45. Recommended Development Strategy

If the application is going to be built using **Next.js + Supabase**, do not ask an AI coding assistant to generate the entire application in one prompt.

Instead, break development into smaller technical phases:

```text
PRD
 ↓
Database Schema
 ↓
ERD
 ↓
Authentication
 ↓
Course Management
 ↓
Payment
 ↓
Enrollment & Authorization
 ↓
Learning Player
 ↓
Progress Tracking
 ↓
Student Dashboard
 ↓
Admin Dashboard
 ↓
Testing
 ↓
Deployment
```

The PRD above should serve as the **master product document**.

Each phase can then have its own **Technical Specification** and **implementation prompt**.
